  ],
  "text": [
    {
      "text": "Students in an introductory psychology course completed an online Stroop task, naming the font colors of words in congruent and incongruent trials.",
      "text_id": 1,
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "section_id": 0,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Being in the incongruent condition caused slower reaction times.",
      "text_id": 2,
      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "section_id": 0,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Here we analyze a Stroop experiment.",
      "text_id": 3,
      "paragraph_id": 2,
      "section_id": 1,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Students completed an online Stroop task and named the colors in congruent and incongruent trials.",
      "text_id": 4,
      "paragraph_id": 2,
      "section_id": 1,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Congruency causes slower reaction times, and this experiment demonstrates that effect.",
      "text_id": 5,
      "paragraph_id": 2,
      "section_id": 1,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Reaction-time tasks of this kind have also been used to study how the presence of other people affects responding in an emergency (Hortensius et al., 2015).",
      "text_id": 6,
      "paragraph_id": 2,
      "section_id": 1,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": "Reaction-time tasks of this kind have also been used to study how the presence of other people affects responding in an emergency <ref type=\"bibr\" target=\"#b0\">(Hortensius et al., 2015)<\/ref>."
    },
    {
      "text": "The mean reaction time of participants in the Congruent condition (M = 15.1, SD = 4.1) was lower than the mean of participants in the Incongruent condition (M = 23.0, SD = 4.78).",
      "text_id": 8,
      "paragraph_id": 4,
      "section_id": 3,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Reaction times in the two conditions were correlated, r = 0.37.",
      "text_id": 9,
      "paragraph_id": 5,
      "section_id": 3,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "A dependent t-test indicated that we could reject the null-hypothesis, t(130) = 18.04, p = .25, Cohen's dz = 0.25.",
      "text_id": 10,
      "paragraph_id": 5,
      "section_id": 3,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "There was also a marginally significant difference in accuracy between conditions, p = .07.",
      "text_id": 11,
      "paragraph_id": 5,
      "section_id": 3,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Accuracy did not differ between congruent and incongruent trials (p = .34), confirming that accuracy was unaffected by congruency.",
      "text_id": 12,
      "paragraph_id": 5,
      "section_id": 3,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "The congruency effect on reaction time was highly significant, p = .000.",
      "text_id": 13,
      "paragraph_id": 6,
      "section_id": 4,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "The Stroop effect did not differ between the students tested in 2013 and in 2014, t(120.37) = -0.42, p = .673.",
      "text_id": 14,
      "paragraph_id": 6,
      "section_id": 4,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "These results confirm the Stroop effect.",
      "text_id": 15,
      "paragraph_id": 7,
      "section_id": 5,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Data and analysis code are available at https://github.com/Lakens/stroop_effect_paper_bad.",
      "text_id": 16,
      "paragraph_id": 7,
      "section_id": 5,
      "page_number": null,
      "formatted": "Data and analysis code are available at <ref type=\"url\" target=\"https://github.com/Lakens/stroop_effect_paper_bad\">https://github.com/Lakens/stroop_effect_paper_bad<\/ref>."
    },
    {
      "text": "Hortensius, R., Schutter, D. J. L. G., & Gelder, B. de. (2015). Personal distress, but not sympathy, predicts the negative influence of bystanders on responding to an emergency. Cognitive, Affective, & Behavioral Neuroscience. https://doi.org/10.3758/s13415-014-0326-3",
      "text_id": 17,
